{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"GHSA-cjq9-62q9-8jv4","published":"2026-10-07T20:30:55Z","modified":"2026-10-07T20:45:06.190363835Z","aliases":["CVE-2026-94483"],"summary":"Next.js has Server-Side Request Forgery in Image Optimization","details":"## Impact\n\nAn attacker-controlled, allow-listed remote URL can lead to server-side request forgery (e.g. to private IPs) during Image Optimization. \n\n## Workaround\n\nAudit allow-listed remote URLs in `images.remotePatterns` (see https://nextjs.org/docs/app/getting-started/images#remote-images) for hosts that may not be trusted with their DNS entries. If no `images.remotePatterns` are configured, your app is not affected.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"next","ecosystem":"npm","purl":"pkg:npm/next"},"ranges":[{"type":"SEMVER","events":[{"introduced":"16.0.0"},{"fixed":"16.3.8"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/advisories/github-reviewed/2026/10/GHSA-cjq9-62q9-8jv4/GHSA-cjq9-62q9-8jv4.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/security/advisories/GHSA-cjq9-62q9-8jv4"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-94483"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/commit/e002ad68bd676bb0ed0c87bb22e3590304763e0b"},{"type":"PACKAGE","url":"https://github.com/vercel/next.js"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/releases/tag/v16.3.8"}],"database_specific":{"cwe_ids":["CWE-918"],"github_reviewed":true,"github_reviewed_at":"2026-10-07T20:30:55Z","nvd_published_at":"2026-10-02T16:16:51Z","severity":"HIGH"},"severity":[{"type":"CVSS_V3","score":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:L/A:N"},{"type":"CVSS_V4","score":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N"}]}